From: Zizheng Guo <zizhengg@nvidia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gfxstream: offer VK_EXT_robustness2 to guests

Zink, Mesa's OpenGL on Vulkan, requires robustness2's nullDescriptor
feature, and the driver offered only the extensions of its allowlist,
which lacked robustness2. The host passes it through.
---
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp	2026-10-01 00:34:46
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp	2026-10-01 00:34:46
@@ -1753,6 +1753,9 @@
         "VK_EXT_load_store_op_none",
         "VK_EXT_swapchain_colorspace",
         "VK_EXT_image_robustness",
+        // Zink, OpenGL on Vulkan, requires robustness2's nullDescriptor.
+        "VK_EXT_robustness2",
+        "VK_KHR_robustness2",
         "VK_EXT_custom_border_color",
         "VK_EXT_border_color_swizzle",
         "VK_EXT_shader_stencil_export",
